          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "The cheapest residential college in Indiana?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "When evaluating total direct costs—which combine full-time tuition, mandatory fees, housing, and a full meal plan—Vincennes University officially ranks as Indiana's lowest-cost residential college, with an average overall direct cost of around $14,500 for in-state students."
          }
        },
